  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Carbon tetrachloride boils at low temperatures and is a non-conductor in both solid and liquid phases.&nbsp;Carbon tetrachloride is made up of individual covalently bonded molecules, CCl<sub>4</sub>. Therefore, the electrons&nbsp;cannot&nbsp;flow and there are&nbsp;no&nbsp;ions. So it&nbsp;does not conduct&nbsp;in any state.</p>",
